Original commit body from f60ad00d38a4cd27b8c0f890b4ad3702e286320a:

main's --backend pre-scan looped `for idx in range(len(argv) - 1)`, so the
last token was never examined: `hypergumbo catalog --backend=tree-sitter`
reached argparse unstripped and exited 2 with "unrecognized arguments",
although the `=` form needs no following token.

Same loop, second defect: because the flag is stripped before argparse
runs, the root parser's `choices=` never applied, so `--backend bogus`
(any position) was silently ignored and the command ran.

The pre-scan moves into `_strip_backend_flag`, which scans every token
(stopping at `--`), reads the value token only when it exists and is not
another option, and rejects a missing value ("expected one argument") or
an unknown one ("invalid choice") through parser.error with argparse's
wording, exit 2. The choices live in one `BACKEND_CHOICES` tuple shared
with the parser's add_argument. No other pre-scanned flag in main has a
lookahead (--debug and --help/--all are membership tests).

